1
00:00:00,245 --> 00:00:02,125
Storms are turning faster,

2
00:00:02,295 --> 00:00:04,645
and the days
are 6 hours long.

3
00:00:04,865 --> 00:00:07,000
The sky has
another problem.

4
00:00:07,515 --> 00:00:10,370
Storms are steered
by the planet's spin,

5
00:00:10,370 --> 00:00:13,575
through the Coriolis
effect, and that steering

6
00:00:13,575 --> 00:00:16,370
grows in step
with the spin rate.

7
00:00:16,453 --> 00:00:20,578
At a 6 hour day it is four
times stronger than today.

8
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:24,800
At the edge of floating,
it is 17 times stronger.

9
00:00:25,187 --> 00:00:27,642
Weather systems
would be squeezed

10
00:00:27,642 --> 00:00:30,742
into tight, fast bands,
and the calm

11
00:00:30,742 --> 00:00:33,872
of an ordinary
afternoon would be gone.

12
00:00:34,098 --> 00:00:35,738
At a 6 hour day,

13
00:00:35,738 --> 00:00:40,188
the Sun races from horizon
to horizon in 3 hours.

14
00:00:40,448 --> 00:00:42,618
The equator
moves at nearly

15
00:00:42,618 --> 00:00:45,438
7,000 kilometers an hour.

16
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:48,230
You are 5.5 percent
lighter.

17
00:00:48,587 --> 00:00:51,592
Jumping now takes
you noticeably higher

18
00:00:51,592 --> 00:00:55,407
than it should, and every
step feels slightly wrong.

19
00:00:55,552 --> 00:00:56,807
Hang on.

20
00:00:56,912 --> 00:00:59,732
If you're enjoying this,
tap like and follow.

21
00:00:59,942 --> 00:01:01,667
Okay, back to the math.

22
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:04,665
And the calendar
is about to break.

23
00:01:04,818 --> 00:01:06,478
Part five of eight.
